ota/sheridan-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 42 of 75 years on the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids. So far in 2026, on that same middle, April to May sat at 52% of normal and March to April at 55%. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, and grid 33419 got down to 50% of normal that year.</p>"}
